WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:06.980
I don't think I've ever had 
a good understanding

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.990
of what I do and don't know.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.910
I don't even know what 
I don't know about men.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.650
I just don't really get it.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.500
Seigi-kun, are you listening?

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.470
Isn't it about time?

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.840
Well, I'm off to my marriage meeting.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.980
<u>Episode 8</u>
<b>The Angel's Aquamarine</b>

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.940
Did you do poorly on a test?

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.250
You look like the world is ending.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.840
Just kill me.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.340
Tanimoto-san's going to a marriage meeting.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.960
Oh, I guess she's already there.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.890
Which means I don't have a chance...

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.860
Go for broke? I'm broke before 
I even went for anything...

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.110
Could you hold on to this for a while?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.370
Are you familiar with 
the words of Machiavelli?

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.810
Machiavelli?

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:13.750
People regret the things they didn't do 
more than the things they did.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.130
They're beautiful!

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.260
They're both gemstones relating to the sea.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.770
Lapis lazuli is also sometimes 
called ultramarine.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.410
"Marine" meaning the sea, 
and "ultra" meaning beyond.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.700
Ultra?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.860
Yes.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.550
The lapis lazuli that was brought 
from Afghanistan to Europe

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.300
was "the blue that came from beyond the sea."

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.070
I see.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:50.930
This aquamarine was mined 
in Santa Maria, Brazil.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.650
The stone's name means "seawater" in Latin.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.390
Sailors have used aquamarines as 
protective charms since ancient times.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:05.530
In addition to signifying good fortune, 
they're also called the angel's stone.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.480
Angel...

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.220
That's perfect for Tanimoto-san.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.610
Did you know that Étranger 
offers an employee discount?

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.530
I'll buy it!

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.080
Seigi.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.470
Are you free tonight?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.740
Yeah, I am.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.510
Then I'll take you to dinner.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.470
You're such a good guy.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.500
But I'll pass tonight.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.560
I see.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.390
Thanks. I really appreciate the thought, but...

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.770
Don't worry about it.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:12.830
Huh?

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.080
Homura-san?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.230
Good to see him looking well.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.470
What... is Tanimoto-san doing here?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.060
Huh?

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.690
Nakata-kun, right?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.450
It's me, Homura. It's been a while.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.650
Hello.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.240
Thank you for your help back then.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.640
Don't mention it.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.940
Um, Homura-san...

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:50.740
Yes?

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:55.160
No... It's nothing.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.670
I'm the one Shoko-chan was meeting.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:06.390
She told me you two are friends from school.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.300
I was surprised.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.800
"Shoko-chan"?

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.540
I've known her for a long time.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.310
Our parents were friends.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.160
<i>Our parents were friends. 
He played with me a lot.</i>

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.860
Yeah, she mentioned it.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.780
I know she said she was 
glad to have a friend

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.100
she could discuss the 
marriage meeting with,

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.600
but she even told you that?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.370
I was surprised. I could hardly believe a 
college student had a marriage meeting.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.120
Our parents are excited about it, but not me.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.090
What about Tanimoto-san? How does she feel?

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.570
Why don't you ask her yourself?

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:47.430
Huh?

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.280
Well, I should get going.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.680
Sorry for holding you up.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.650
Seigi-kun, are you listening?

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.550
Isn't it about time?

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.730
Well, I'm off.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:15.120
Huh?

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.540
Wait, Tanimoto-san...

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.790
Don't go!

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.550
Just a dream...

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.630
Tanimoto-san!

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:01.580
Seigi-kun.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:06.130
I heard you know Homura-san.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.080
What a surprise.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.950
Oh, yeah...

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:12.340
Seigi-kun?

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.480
Um, Tanimoto-san...

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:22.230
About Homura-san...
Do you really want to marry him?

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.560
Why?

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.570
Why? Because, uh...

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:36.030
I guess you could say...
I'm worried about you.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:44.460
I don't really know what it 
means to be with a man.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.430
Huh?

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.430
I like Homura-san.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.210
Like how I like my dad or mom.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.340
But I don't know what it means 
to like someone in a different way.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:58.930
Someone I thought was a friend once said to me,

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.720
"I like you. Please go out with me."

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:08.770
We were having so much fun as just friends, 
but I guess that wasn't enough.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.780
Well, once I get married,

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:16.660
I won't have to worry about 
romance anymore, right?

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:19.910
So I want to get married.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.440
I'm the worst, aren't I?

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:30.990
Sometimes I see myself as a gemstone 
that was mistakenly put on display.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.760
Among beryls, there are 
aquamarines containing iron,

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.950
emeralds containing chromium,

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:41.220
and goshenite containing 
nothing at all, right?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:47.190
But since colorless, transparent aquamarines 
and goshenite look the same,

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.730
goshenite is often put on 
display as aquamarine...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:56.800
even though it's a totally different 
beryl that contains no iron.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.340
Just like how choosing not to fall in love

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:04.450
and never understanding it in 
the first place aren't the same.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.870
Maybe that's how love works, 
but I think marriage is different.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.360
Huh?

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.360
My mom's a divorcée.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.930
My dad was an awful guy.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:25.520
She's remarried now, 
but she probably did it for me.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:29.390
I think it's okay for some 
marriages to be like that.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.770
If someone says otherwise, then...

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.400
Then?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.400
Then they're...

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.240
They're probably the kind of person 
who'd say gemstones are all the same.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.870
Even though they're all one of a kind.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:53.920
Do you remember what you 
said about me, Seigi-kun?

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.670
<i>How cool...</i>

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:00.720
That made me way happier 
than being called cute or pretty.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.790
I wish you all the best.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.300
Thank you, Seigi-kun.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.400
I've decided to support her.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.410
Support who?

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:27.150
I'm going to support 
Tanimoto-san's marriage meetings.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.040
It's really for the best.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.830
May I offer my thoughts?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.480
Go ahead.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.090
You fool.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.470
Say whatever you want.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.120
I've already made up my mind.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:48.600
The best thing I can do isn't asking her out.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:53.700
She's on a date with Homura-san 
at the science museum right now.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.190
It's for the best.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:00.580
If you're free tonight, Richard,
let's go out together.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.310
We can toast to Tanimoto-san's happiness.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.240
I guess you'll be having a parfait...

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.200
Shiseido Parlour

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:16.070
Seigi, let me tell you an interesting story.

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:18.730
You're ignoring me?

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:22.730
Long ago, somewhere in England,

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:26.070
there lived a boy with a very beautiful face.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.020
No matter what he did,

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:37.230
he was cursed to always have 
people talk about his face.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:47.180
One day, he met a girl.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.660
They met in the Japanese department.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:54.210
Seeing the boy so concerned about his face, 
she said to him quite plainly,

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.330
"Don't worry about it."

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.230
He'd never met anyone like her before.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.900
It didn't take long for him to fall in love.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:12.720
But the boy bore a second curse:

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.510
his great-grandfather's inheritance.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.900
Faced with such tremendous wealth, 
the girl said the following:

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:27.410
"I'm scared I'd choose the money 
if something happened."

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.350
"I'd rather break up than 
be that kind of person."

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:42.550
Question: if you were him, 
how would you have responded to her?

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:48.800
I'd like to tell her not to worry about 
it and to stay with me forever.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.760
But that's hard to say...

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.760
It is.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:57.770
But even without the inheritance, 
if she wanted to break up,

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:01.020
clinging to her would've 
only made him miserable.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:05.400
Therefore, he chose silence.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.280
He didn't say anything?

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:13.910
That's why I shared Machiavelli's 
words with you the other day.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:19.540
We regret the things we don't do 
more than the things we did.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.770
That's right.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:28.820
If I were you, I'd be running to her 
instead of sitting around here.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:35.390
Do you realize? You often 
compliment my appearance,

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.360
but you have trouble expressing affection

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:41.470
for those you don't wish to dislike you.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:46.400
You mentioned before that you 
were afraid of being disliked.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.870
But hasn't it been long enough?

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:52.460
It's time to forget the cowardly hero of justice.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:53.280
Huh?

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.790
Seigi, abandon your vanity and shame.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:03.270
Aren't you the man who follows his heart 
and embraces his inborn meddlesomeness

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:10.130
in order to lead the people around 
him toward bright futures?

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.280
Go to the science museum.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.440
I really like you.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.280
I like you very much as well, Seigi.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.950
I'm glad to have met you.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.940
From the moment we met until now. 
That hasn't changed.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.500
If you're still open by the time I'm done, 
I'll be back at mach speed.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.770
At least invite her out to dinner.

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:44.720
Yeah.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.270
<i>Richard once told me...</i>

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:16.940
<i>that gemstones lead people to 
the answers they truly desire.</i>

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.040
Huh? Seigi-kun?

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.630
Shoko-chan, I'm going to make a call.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.820
Okay.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.970
What a surprise.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:42.980
Tanimoto-san, I...

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:49.350
The other day, I said I thought it was okay
 for some marriages to be that way.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:53.260
That I'd support your decision.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.490
But I'm sorry... I can't after all.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.350
Seigi-kun?

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.500
An aquamarine...

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:13.510
I've been wanting to give it to you.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.190
To me?

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:16.080
Yeah.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:19.850
The moment Richard 
showed me this aquamarine,

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:23.310
I thought it was perfect for you.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.330
You're like an angel.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:33.940
To me, that's the kind of person you are.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:39.690
Seigi-kun, you mean this is how you see me?

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.690
Yeah.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.500
I don't think all gemstones are the same.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:50.820
But in the near future, 
you might find someone you like.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:54.260
You might want to fall in love.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.320
I don't think you have to give up on that yet.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.350
So... So I...

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:07.100
I don't want you to get married.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:21.950
I probably would've blown that off 
if it came from anyone else.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.370
But since it's you, Seigi-kun...

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.090
I want to thank you.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.340
You really are a hero of justice.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:40.770
Huh?

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:44.430
Seigi-kun, do you remember 
when we first met?

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:47.350
Of course I do.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:52.110
When things aren't going well 
for me or my head feels foggy,

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.720
I like to help those in need.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:19:00.200
I pretend to be a good person
to feel better about myself.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:04.030
But imagine my surprise when 
a <i>real</i> nice person showed up.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.710
My kindness is self-satisfaction, 
but you're different.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:17.050
You're someone who hears cries 
for help and extends a hand.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.930
I'm not...

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:23.690
Seigi-kun, you remembered what 
I said the other day, didn't you?

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:28.840
After talking about it,

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:33.730
I felt I couldn't get married 
to run away from something.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.900
If I did that, I wouldn't like myself.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:38.990
I wouldn't be able to forgive myself.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.000
So...

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:42.440
So?

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:45.530
I'm going to turn down Homura-san.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:49.790
You helped me realize my feelings.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.290
Thank you, Seigi-kun.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.850
You really are cool, Tanimoto-san.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.930
You're a coward.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.440
I know. I hate myself.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.370
Next time, you'd better tell her you like her.

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:29.580
By the way, I received a call 
from Richard-san the other day.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.320
Where's he going?

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:36.580
Where? What do you mean?

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:40.710
Isn't Étranger going to be closed 
for a while starting tomorrow?

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:43.580
Étranger's closing?

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.220
I haven't heard anything about that.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.850
You should call the store.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.050
It's Seigi.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:59.170
<i>How did it go?</i>

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:03.520
Well, it didn't go horribly.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:07.760
I failed to ask her out to dinner, 
but I'll tell you all about it when I get back.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.950
<i>You needn't come back today.</i>

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.070
What? Why not?

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:16.580
<i>Now that I think about it, 
we've known each other for some time now.</i>

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.130
Huh? What are you saying?

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:22.640
<i>I've paid your salary in full.</i>

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.720
<i>Don't worry about the rest.</i>

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.960
What are you talking about?

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:28.660
<i>One last thing...</i>

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.340
Wait.

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:32.220
I'm on my way back to the store now.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.820
Notice

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:44.070
<i>You trust people too much.</i>

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:50.780
<i>Sometimes it hurts you, 
but that's how life is.</i>

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:51.810
Are you alive?
What happened?

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.950
<i>Remember that.</i>

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.950
Richard

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.950
Are you alive?
What happened?

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.720
<i>Farewell.</i>

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:58.440
<i>The number you have called is 
either outside the service area</i>

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:00.150
<i>or has been turned off.</i>

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.880
That idiot...

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.470
<b>North Wing Departures</b>
